        "original_id": "3e075c58-6b27-528f-8271-685005bf9c6b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Siegi Sessler, Freddie Sessler, Bette Davis, Frank Sinatra, Humphrey Bogart, Bob Hope, Bing Crosby, David Niven, Marlon Brando, Marilyn Monroe, John Wayne, Cary Grant, Clark Gable, Doris Day, Joan Crawford, Ingrid Bergman, Elizabeth Taylor, Keith Richards\n- Roles: Actress, restaurateur, club owner\n- Organizations: The Rolling Stones\n- Topics: Hollywood stars, celebrity clientele, family relationships, drug supply\n\nFacts:\n- Bette Davis was born on April 5, 1908, and she was an American film, television, and theater actress with Welsh ancestry.\n- Freddie Sessler was born on May 26, 1923, and he was the brother of London restaurateur and club owner Siegi Sessler.\n- A place associated with Siegi Sessler was well known as a \"home away from home\" for Hollywood stars including Frank Sinatra, Humphrey Bogart, Bob Hope, Bing Crosby, David Niven, Marlon Brando, Marilyn Monroe, John Wayne, Cary Grant, Bette Davis, Clark Gable, Doris Day, Joan Crawford, Ingrid Bergman, and Elizabeth Taylor.\n- Freddie Sessler was a long-term intimate of the Rolling Stones, especially Keith Richards, and he supplied drugs to Keith Richards.\n- Bette Davis died on October 6, 1989.\n- Freddie Sessler died on December 18, 2000.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
